PATCH 216: reconstruct FUN_0000_8744 (a DCBS per-type object INIT method dispatched by c296's tail
near-vector, object-type 1) -- the next DGROUP-near-offset base-loss in the DCBS object-init family.
Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x8744-0x8790.

Reached after patch 215: c296 dispatches the enemy roster record 1 (di=0xc157 = 0xc05c+0xfb) to its
per-type init method word[DGROUP:(word[di]*2-0x1b20)] = 0x8744 (type 1).  8744 was pristine Ghidra:
`*(param_1+0xad)=2` etc. with param_1 = di (0xc157) treated as a HOST pointer -> SIGSEGV (observed live:
`d81e->43c1->c296->8744 param_1=0xc157`, deterministic under COOP_TICK).  DS=DGROUP=0x1c00; every [di+N]
is a DS-relative byte/word field (asm movw/movb at the raw byte offsets 0xad/0xbb/0xaf/0xb1/0xb3/0xfa/
0x8d/0x87/0x14/0xb5/0xb6/0x16 -- NO /2 scaling here, unlike c296).  The tail copies a seg-0x2c9f template
into the object body at DGROUP:di+0xbc via 1e27 (near-offset dst which 1e27 bases internally, patch 087).
Reconstructed with the explicit DGROUP base + the asm byte/word widths.

